extraction_notes: "WB13 Lone Star printed 98-100 (cache p099-p101, cache page = printed folio + 1): the Psi-X Aliens introduction and the R.C.C. heading are on 98, natural abilities, bonuses, attacks, penalties and the psi-power table on 99, the last table entry, I.S.P., disposition, skills and equipment on 100, where Notable CS Characters begins. All numbers read off 170 dpi renders; printed 100 was read from the render only, its text layer being welded across both columns. || HEADING: Psi-X Alien R.C.C., Race: Genetically Altered Human, tagged Optional Player Character. The entry does not send the character to an O.C.C. and does not call for a roll on the Human Special Abilities table of printed 97. || XP: the ladder headed Psi-X Alien, Xiticix Killer on the unnumbered Experience Tables page after printed 174 (cache p176). || ATTRIBUTES as printed: I.Q. 3D6+6 (but special, see skills), M.E. 3D6, M.A. 2D6 (+2 if a good alignment: text), P.S. 2D4+4, P.P. 2D4+4, P.E. 2D4+1, P.B. 2D4+2, Spd 2D6+4. || POOLS: hit points P.E. x2 plus 1D6 per level. S.D.C. is printed as 2D6+2 and nothing else - no P.E. term and no plus-those-gained-from-skills wording - so it is the whole figure and is stored as sdc_base with no men_of_arms line (judgement; the entry takes no O.C.C. whose pool it could override). P.P.E. is printed P.E. x10. || PSIONICS: every Psi-X has See Aura, Sense Magic, Detect Psionics and Bio-Regeneration (healing, stored as the Healing power, not the Super one); see the invisible is printed among the vision abilities as automatic and is natural-ability text. Printed 98-100 state no psychic tier and no save target; master is stored because the power packages include Super powers, which only a master holds. Random Psi-Powers is a percentile table stored as a choice of one of nine abilities, each carrying its named powers. The printed ranges leave 98-00 for Mind Melter and skip nothing. Kinetesis: the six named powers plus Telekinesis; the book says all kinesis abilities. Psi-Sensitive and Healer say all sensitive / all healing powers: stored as the catalog rows whose source is the Rifts core book (23 Sensitive, 15 Healing); doubled range, doubled Healing Touch and +30% exorcism are text. Energy Conduit''s imperviousness to fire and Closed Mind''s immunities are text. Intuitive prints presence sense evil with no comma; stored as Presence Sense and Sense Evil. Spiritualist''s +20% to find the way home is text. Mind Melter is printed as two words and an exclamation mark; no powers stored. || I.S.P. is a second percentile table stored as a choice of one of five abilities, each carrying its isp_base: M.E. x10 +8 per level, M.E. x5 +2D6, M.E. x2 +12, M.E. x3 +1D6, M.E. +4D6 per level. || BONUSES: +5 save vs horror factor, +5 save vs magic illusions (illusionary_magic). || ATTACKS: One physical at levels 1, 2, 4, 8 and 12, or two via psionics at levels 1, 3, 6, 10 and 15. Stored as attacks_base 1 and +1 at levels 2, 4, 8 and 12; the psionic ladder is text. No hand to hand is printed. || SKILLS (O.C.C. Skills of Psi-X Aliens): two languages of choice at 98%, stored as two picks of Language: Other at base 98. Then select ONE skill category, all those skills known at +20%: stored as nine variants, one per printed category, each adding the catalog''s Rifts skills of that category at catalog base + 20 (Communications 19, Electrical 5, Mechanical 13, Medical 19, Pilot Related 7, Rogue 15, Science 20, Technical: Languages and Lores 42, Technical: Others 45 on the day of import). Technical is printed as two choices: languages and lores (all), and others (all, except language and lore); rows named Language or Lore went to the first, every other Technical row including literacy to the second. Left out: the generic rows Language: Other, Language: Native Tongue and Literacy: Other (a tongue with no row of its own is taken at +20% by hand), and three skills the catalog marks exclusive to another O.C.C. (Professional Restoration, Recognize Authenticity, Recognize Machine Quality). Also left out of Science: the analytical chemistry skill, whose catalog name carries an em-dash that a pure-ASCII class file cannot spell; it is known at 45% (25 + 20) and is added by hand. R.C.C. Related Skills: None, so no related block. Secondary: four, no bonuses, from domestic, pilot and W.P. at level one and one more at levels 3, 5, 9 and 11. || EQUIPMENT: survival knife, one energy weapon of choice (the catalog''s energy-weapon-of-choice row), 1D4 additional E-clips, backpack, knapsack, utility belt, air filter, protective eye goggles, universal translator (portable language translator row), cigarette lighter, note pad, canteen. No armor is listed; may use light armor is a restriction line. || MONEY: none printed, none stored. || Penalties, insanity (three phobias and one obsession), one-third endurance and addiction are side_effects. Disposition is lore."
---

## Lore

The Psi-X are what came of Desmond Bradford''s private, illegal attempt to
find the genetic root of psychic power and switch it on. His subjects were
human, many of them teenagers taken against their will, and he spliced
Psi-Stalker and D-Bee material into them on little more than a hunch. The
psionics arrived. So did a body that never fills out, a hairless oversized
head and a pair of huge dark eyes; one of the first victims said he had been
made into a saucer alien, and the name stuck.

Bradford counts them his worst personal failure, but could not bring himself
to put down people the way the labs put down animals. More than 150 were
quietly turned loose in the Pecos Badlands, where most survived and have
started families.

A Psi-X drifts a few feet off the ground rather than walking, sees almost
everything except a bright afternoon, and leans on its mind for nearly all it
does. Each is brilliant inside one narrow field and hopeless outside it. Good
ones tend to be sunny and guileless, selfish ones sly and boastful, and the
evil ones brooding, cruel and trusting of nobody.

## GM Notes

Two percentile rolls define the character: the psi-power package and the
I.S.P. level. Both are stored as choices, so roll and then pick the entry
rolled. A result of 98-00 on the power table says only Mind Melter; assign
that O.C.C.''s powers yourself.

Pick the one skill category with the class. Every skill in it is known at
+20%; outside it the character has two languages and a few secondary skills
and can learn nothing else.

The sheet counts the physical attack ladder. A Psi-X fighting with its mind
uses the other one: two psionic attacks at level 1, with two more at levels
3, 6, 10 and 15. Add +2 M.A. for a good alignment by hand.

Play the drawbacks: day vision of 40 feet, eyes that must stay covered, three
phobias and an obsession, a third of human stamina, and a weakness for drink
and drugs. Bio-manipulation and empathic transmission hit them twice as hard
for twice as long.
